WEBVTT

00:00:01.380 --> 00:00:04.400
<i>Main is ecstatic that they finish 
making some colored inks.</i>

00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:05.600
<i>But...</i>

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:11.350
Upon the high priest's orders, 
Dirk has been adopted by a noble.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:12.060
What?

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.700
More importantly, Lady Main,

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:16.950
please be cautious of the high priest.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:21.090
The high priest was involved 
in the incident at the east gate.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.050
<i>Then the curtain rises on even more trouble.</i>

00:00:29.430 --> 00:00:32.080
Main! We've come to get you.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:34.640
Tuuli, what brings you here?

00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:37.670
Let's go home together. It's been 
dangerous lately, hasn't it?

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.020
I'll protect you, Main!

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:42.470
Me, too! I'll protect you, Lady Main!

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:44.960
Um...

00:00:46.700 --> 00:00:50.020
It's dangerous for me to have 
more of you to protect...

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:52.990
So, listen, Tuuli.

00:00:52.990 --> 00:00:56.860
If something were to happen, 
you'd be in more danger than I am.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:00.570
If it were just me, 
Sir Damuel could protect me.

00:01:00.570 --> 00:01:02.490
Fine, I got it.

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:05.530
Lady Main had just gone home.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:07.210
Damn it... Main!

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:10.040
They let a carriage through?!

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.660
Is it the one from the other day?

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:14.960
Yeah, it's the same noble.

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.930
I'm surprised you know about this.

00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:19.510
We're looking for him right now.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.180
You contacted the knights, didn't you?

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:25.990
Huh? Um... I'm not sure...

00:01:26.230 --> 00:01:30.480
The captain went to the cathedral 
to make sure Main was okay.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.230
You didn't bump into him?

00:01:32.830 --> 00:01:33.760
Rot!

00:01:38.850 --> 00:01:41.450
Could something have happened to Lady Main?

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:46.520
We'll definitely be safe with 
the knights here, right, Tuuli?

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:49.720
Tuuli?

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:55.820
H-Help me...

00:01:57.550 --> 00:01:58.720
Did something happen?

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.560
Captain!

00:01:59.920 --> 00:02:01.050
Where's Main?

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:14.250
What do you think... you're 
doing to my daughter?!

00:02:14.770 --> 00:02:15.740
Ow!

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:16.560
Main!

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.610
Lady Main!

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.770
Are you okay, Main?

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:22.770
Yes. Where's Tuuli?

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.740
N-No...

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.250
Main?

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.280
Lady Main?

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:35.330
Hey. What do you think 
you're doing to my Tuuli?

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:51.520
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.030
<b>Ascendance of a Bookworm</b>

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:16.980
<b>Chapter Thirty-Five
The Black Protective Charm</b>

00:04:21.690 --> 00:04:24.140
Get your dirty hands off of Tuuli.

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:28.170
Or you're going to die. I mean it.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.440
Tuuli!

00:04:36.440 --> 00:04:38.580
I-I was so scared.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:46.170
<i>A magic stone?</i>

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:48.440
Dad, look out!

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:49.970
Getilgt!

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:54.630
I'll take care of things here.

00:04:54.630 --> 00:04:58.000
Gunther, return to the cathedral and inform 
Lord Ferdinand of what's going on!

00:04:58.000 --> 00:04:58.760
Yes, sir.

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.310
Otto, take care of Main!

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:03.500
Main, we should also...

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:05.110
You're bleeding, Main.

00:05:06.100 --> 00:05:08.660
Must be from when I was dropped earlier.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:14.270
Mister Otto, we're definitely in trouble 
right now, and we need to call for help, right?

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.490
What else could this possibly seem like to you?

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:26.520
If you're ever in trouble, press your 
blood seal upon this black stone.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:28.370
If I'm in trouble?

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:29.560
Yes.

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:32.230
I promise I'll come save you.

00:05:40.220 --> 00:05:41.870
Main, what is that?

00:05:41.870 --> 00:05:42.790
A protective charm.

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:43.790
Let's hurry!

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:51.780
The head priest is currently not in.

00:05:51.780 --> 00:05:54.030
What? Where did he go?

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:55.300
No idea.

00:05:55.300 --> 00:05:57.400
Then if you could give him a message for me.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:59.700
We've received word from Master Gunther

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:02.050
that the noble from the other 
day has made it into the city.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:03.980
Received. If you'll excuse me.

00:06:07.070 --> 00:06:08.030
Fran.

00:06:09.410 --> 00:06:11.730
Is Lady Main around?

00:06:11.730 --> 00:06:17.420
Dirk's new father is here and 
would like to speak with her.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.930
Lady Main has gone home.

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.930
The head priest is also out.

00:06:21.930 --> 00:06:24.330
I see. What a pity.

00:06:29.440 --> 00:06:33.270
<i>We had Tuuli and Lutz stay behind 
at the Gilberta Company,</i>

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:36.210
<i>and we headed to the cathedral.</i>

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.450
He's absent?

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:42.630
Yes. The head priest is currently not here.

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:43.630
I see...

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.040
An emergency flare had gone up,

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.470
so he might have been 
summoned by the knights.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.070
I see.

00:06:51.070 --> 00:06:56.360
Also, apparently Dirk's new father 
is here and wanted to see you.

00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:57.490
See me?

00:06:57.490 --> 00:06:58.650
Yes.

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:01.140
I was relieved that you didn't have to go

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:06.500
to the high priest's room 
while the head priest is out.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:08.430
Sir Damuel.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.190
Is Lord Ferdinand here?

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:11.960
Huh?

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:15.290
I used ordonnanz, but he didn't reply.

00:07:15.290 --> 00:07:17.250
That's why I came here.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:20.160
I figured he went to see the knights.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.410
Then where exactly is the head priest?

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.850
Let's speak with Arno one more time.

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:29.590
Yes.

00:07:30.440 --> 00:07:34.170
Apprentice Priestess,
put this on just in case.

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:37.430
The ring that one of the men was using 
earlier that'll serve as evidence.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:43.940
Unlike Lord Ferdinand, I have 
no magic stones to lend you.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:46.980
I thank you kindly for your consideration.

00:07:51.160 --> 00:07:53.820
What? The size isn't changing.

00:07:55.750 --> 00:07:58.450
It does seem to let me store 
my mana in it at least.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.330
Let's go.

00:08:04.920 --> 00:08:08.450
Please... Watch over Lady Main.

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:14.800
Here is proof of the contract.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:15.470
Yes, sir.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:21.360
This completes our contract.

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.500
This way.

00:08:42.570 --> 00:08:44.360
I've been searching for you, Main.

00:08:44.820 --> 00:08:46.240
Damn it, why?

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:51.080
Count Bindewald, that's the blue 
apprentice priestess, Main.

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:52.250
Oho...

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.750
Main, I will establish a contract with you.

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:04.780
A contract?

00:09:04.780 --> 00:09:08.930
How lovely to have a noble 
fancy you, Lady Main.

00:09:09.310 --> 00:09:14.410
You'll be adopted by Count 
Bindewald... just like Dirk.

00:09:15.260 --> 00:09:18.870
The contract I formed with that 
infant is one of servitude.

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:19.840
What?

00:09:22.170 --> 00:09:24.530
But it says right here that 
you've adopted him...

00:09:24.530 --> 00:09:26.290
Take a look at the second form.

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:31.370
A Devouring servitude contract?

00:09:31.960 --> 00:09:34.800
The Devouring refers to a 
commoner who has mana.

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:37.020
In exchange for a magic item,

00:09:37.020 --> 00:09:42.050
they are forced into a life 
of servitude until they die.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:46.540
No... You're lying. She's lying, right?

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:50.820
You said you'd make sure 
we could stay together.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.480
Yes, that child will be mine.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:57.330
But in exchange, Main will 
leave the cathedral.

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.090
What?

00:09:58.850 --> 00:10:00.570
Those are the terms of this deal.

00:10:00.570 --> 00:10:02.110
I've heard nothing of this!

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:05.080
There is no contract unless 
all parties agree!

00:10:06.390 --> 00:10:08.890
Well, this is a servitude contract.

00:10:08.890 --> 00:10:11.320
Because of the Spring 
Prayer as well as today,

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:15.790
I've lost many of my Devouring soldiers.

00:10:15.790 --> 00:10:19.140
I'll have you make up for my loss yourself.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.950
Now, sign the contract!

00:10:21.310 --> 00:10:24.160
The head priest is currently gone.

00:10:24.160 --> 00:10:28.200
I will just turn a blind eye if 
you decide to run off with Main.

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:32.100
Capture her quickly and leave 
the city, Count Bindewald.

00:10:33.780 --> 00:10:36.620
You may kill anyone besides the child.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:37.930
Capture her!

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.080
Apprentice Priestess! Step back!

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.450
Schwert!

00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:53.860
What? Who is that?

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:57.080
That is Lady Main's knight bodyguard
 that I'd informed you of.

00:10:57.080 --> 00:10:59.550
Knight bodyguard? I know nothing of this!

00:10:59.550 --> 00:11:02.000
The knights finding about 
this would not be good.

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:06.140
Look out!

00:11:08.370 --> 00:11:11.020
You insolent little commoner Devouring girl.

00:11:22.430 --> 00:11:26.290
Oho, so you already have 
on a ring of servitude.

00:11:27.350 --> 00:11:28.950
A ring of servitude?

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:34.450
As long as you have that ring on, 
you cannot attack your master.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.540
You cannot take that ring off unless 
the contract is annulled.

00:11:38.870 --> 00:11:42.310
Meaning this ring is worthless 
unless a contract is formed.

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.260
You won't be able to run that insolent 
little mouth for much longer!

00:11:51.050 --> 00:11:52.070
Dirk!

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:57.060
What a pity. Infants don't 
have much mana after all.

00:11:58.660 --> 00:12:02.120
How cruel... How dare you do that to Dirk?!

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:07.180
Are you able to attack a defenseless infant?

00:12:07.180 --> 00:12:10.500
Are you willing to throw Delia 
into the depths of despair?

00:12:10.500 --> 00:12:12.440
Please! Please no!

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:14.200
Lady Main, please!

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:20.220
No!

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:22.720
Yes! Well done, Jenni!

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:23.790
Main!

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:26.330
Let go of me!

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:27.380
I will not.

00:12:28.030 --> 00:12:31.980
I'm being forced to work as a flower-giver

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:36.610
while Rosina and Wilma get to continue 
on like nothing has changed.

00:12:37.580 --> 00:12:39.370
That's hardly fair, is it?

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.100
You're more trouble than you're worth.

00:12:45.150 --> 00:12:46.110
Messer.

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:50.880
Open up your hand.

00:12:50.880 --> 00:12:51.750
No!

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:55.360
Ow!

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:58.850
Now, let's get your blood seal.

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.380
No, no!

00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:06.970
No, no, no!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:10.890
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:13:13.050 --> 00:13:16.980
<b>Ascendance of a
 Bookworm</b>

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:18.850
No!

00:13:19.600 --> 00:13:20.730
No!

00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:22.610
No!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.490
No!

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:25.990
No!

00:13:26.510 --> 00:13:27.480
I don't want to!

00:13:27.950 --> 00:13:28.980
Stop it!

00:13:29.210 --> 00:13:30.480
No!

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:31.870
Let go of Main!

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:36.540
Main, are you all right?

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:40.050
You insolent peasant!

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:42.930
Dad!

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:45.950
This is... nothing...

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:47.160
Dad!

00:13:47.160 --> 00:13:49.360
Dad! Dad!

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.320
You won't get away with this.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:01.100
Count Bindewald!

00:14:03.270 --> 00:14:06.030
Don't think the same trick will keep working!

00:14:10.270 --> 00:14:13.290
I'm not scared of you, child!

00:14:24.340 --> 00:14:27.630
This is a magic stone of 
darkness that absorbs mana!

00:14:32.020 --> 00:14:34.030
Futile! Absolutely futile!

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:42.430
What?

00:14:54.460 --> 00:14:56.710
Wh-What's the meaning of this?

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:05.980
Main!

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.210
Just how much...

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.150
I let my guard down...

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:22.610
To think she possessed this much mana.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:26.230
Apprentice Priestess!

00:15:28.490 --> 00:15:29.740
Sir Damuel!

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:34.000
How pathetic to call yourself a knight
 when you have so little mana.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:54.420
Head Priest!

00:15:54.740 --> 00:15:56.480
What is the meaning of this?

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.370
What are you doing here?

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.940
You should be away.

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:07.430
I'd announced that I was away...

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:12.940
But it appears as though a stranger 
has entered the cathedral.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:16.440
High Priest, who is this?

00:16:16.900 --> 00:16:19.210
A noble from Ahrensbach!

00:16:19.510 --> 00:16:21.690
If you could kindly show me your permit.

00:16:21.930 --> 00:16:25.210
Why must I show anything to a mere priest?

00:16:25.530 --> 00:16:27.650
Well, since our lord is currently away,

00:16:27.650 --> 00:16:30.710
no noble from another domain 
is allowed to enter this city.

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:33.970
Are you trying to suggest 
that I forged my permit?

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:36.720
He has been granted proper permission.

00:16:37.010 --> 00:16:40.540
We had established some 
new rules this winter.

00:16:40.540 --> 00:16:42.570
Were you not aware of them?

00:16:42.570 --> 00:16:44.890
New rules?

00:16:45.250 --> 00:16:47.730
Ah... Please forgive me.

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.940
The winter social is for nobles.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:54.000
Of course, you wouldn't know.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:58.310
M-More importantly, do something about Main!

00:16:58.310 --> 00:17:00.490
I'm not the one who caused all this trouble!

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:01.760
It was Main!

00:17:01.760 --> 00:17:02.630
What?

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.210
I was viciously attacked.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:09.370
She had the nerve to attack 
me, a noble, with her mana.

00:17:09.370 --> 00:17:13.260
Capture Main for committing 
treason against a noble!

00:17:14.020 --> 00:17:16.940
Main, you let your mana go berserk again?

00:17:16.940 --> 00:17:18.930
It was an emergency.

00:17:18.930 --> 00:17:20.250
I can see that.

00:17:21.590 --> 00:17:25.770
Head Priest... am I going 
to be charged with a crime?

00:17:25.770 --> 00:17:26.690
Yes.

00:17:27.080 --> 00:17:30.220
Because we are dealing with the high 
priest and a noble from another domain.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:36.400
Not just yourself, but your family and 
your attendants will all be charged.

00:17:37.100 --> 00:17:38.840
I'm sorry, Dad.

00:17:38.840 --> 00:17:42.710
I was prepared to die as soon as 
you started going to the cathedral.

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:45.270
This is no different.

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:55.130
Lord Sylvester, you liar.

00:17:55.130 --> 00:17:57.550
You promised to protect me.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.810
Main, where did you get that?

00:18:01.130 --> 00:18:03.590
He gave it to me after he went hunting.

00:18:03.590 --> 00:18:05.420
He said it was a protective charm.

00:18:06.990 --> 00:18:08.180
I see.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:11.930
That is a powerful protective charm indeed.

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:13.810
What do you mean by that?

00:18:14.120 --> 00:18:15.230
That's only...

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:20.040
if you are prepared to become 
Sylvester's daughter.

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:25.940
You mean Lord Sylvester 
instead of Lord Karstedt?

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:27.040
Correct.

00:18:28.070 --> 00:18:29.940
But not in two years.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.460
This would be immediately.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:33.360
Huh?

00:18:34.310 --> 00:18:38.540
If you have that resolve, you'll 
be able to save your family.

00:18:45.990 --> 00:18:49.720
Absolutely not. You're not 
leaving us immediately!

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.850
If that is how to save everyone...

00:19:05.100 --> 00:19:06.600
Then I will proceed.

00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:07.240
Main!

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:13.220
I want to protect everyone.

00:19:14.150 --> 00:19:16.000
Please forgive me, Dad.

00:19:16.790 --> 00:19:18.230
Main...

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:25.430
If you've made up your mind...

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:28.670
Main, pray to the wind and protect them.

00:19:29.350 --> 00:19:32.510
Protect them from my mana.

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:35.320
From your mana?

00:19:37.200 --> 00:19:40.130
We've just received this justification.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:43.770
I will now take this moment to be 
rid of those who stand in my way.

00:19:43.770 --> 00:19:47.230
Head Priest, have you 
sealed away Main's mana?

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:50.580
Let Count Bindewald dispose of that vermin.

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:53.480
It's best to throw her out of this domain.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.120
What do you think you're doing?

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:02.010
Wh-What are you doing?!

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:05.520
You dying right now will 
just cause me issues later.

00:20:05.520 --> 00:20:10.390
What?! Quit fooling around and untie me!

00:20:11.130 --> 00:20:13.800
Are you defying my orders?!

00:20:14.200 --> 00:20:17.320
Why does a priest have a schtappe?

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:23.790
Why... it's because I am a noble who 
graduated from the Royal Academy, of course,

00:20:23.790 --> 00:20:25.320
Count Bindewald.

00:20:26.930 --> 00:20:31.000
You may think it's safe for 
you once you leave Ehrenfest,

00:20:32.010 --> 00:20:35.430
but don't think for a second 
I'm letting you escape.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:48.740
Goddess of Wind that rules 
over protection, Schutzaria,

00:20:49.600 --> 00:20:52.920
and the twelve kindred 
goddesses at her side...

00:20:53.630 --> 00:20:58.360
Hear my prayer and grant me holy power!

00:20:58.760 --> 00:21:03.360
Grant me a shield of wind that will 
ward away those who wish to do us harm!

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:21.560
<i>Everyone here... My family...</i>

00:21:21.560 --> 00:21:23.290
<i>I'm going to protect them!</i>

00:22:56.930 --> 00:22:59.940
<b>Next Chapter
Blessing</b>

00:22:59.930 --> 00:23:03.890
Jeez, you should've saved 
us earlier, Head Priest.

00:23:03.890 --> 00:23:06.250
I didn't know what was going on. 
There's no helping that.

00:23:06.250 --> 00:23:08.890
Well, since you came out of your quarters,

00:23:08.890 --> 00:23:10.920
you must have been in your secret room.

00:23:10.920 --> 00:23:15.320
Correct. I was doing some research 
regarding this current incident.

00:23:15.320 --> 00:23:20.670
Sir Damuel mentioned he used
 ordonnanz, but you didn't reply.

00:23:20.670 --> 00:23:23.510
Ordonnanz doesn't reach my hidden room.

00:23:23.510 --> 00:23:25.900
Then how did you find out what was going on?

00:23:25.900 --> 00:23:30.540
Zahm had delivered a magic message
from the knight at the north gate to me.

00:23:30.540 --> 00:23:34.660
I see... Wait, what's a magic message?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:39.970
Illustration by: Katsuki Hikaru
